ns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that can be used as an event handler"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const handler = createHotkeyHandler('Mod+S', (event, { hotkey, parsedHotkey }) => {\n  console.log(`${hotkey} was pressed`)\n  handleSave()\n})\n\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', handler)","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"hotkey","text":"hotkey","level":3},{"id":"callback","text":"callback","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createHotkeyHandler(\n   hotkey, \n   callback, \n   options?): (event) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [match.ts:87](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/match.ts#L87)\n\nCreates a keyboard event handler that calls the callback when the hotkey matches.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### hotkey\n\n  \\| [`Hotkey`](../type-aliases/Hotkey.md)\n  \\| [`ParsedHotkey`](../type-aliases/ParsedHotkey.md)\n\nThe hotkey string or ParsedHotkey to match\n\n### callback\n\n[`HotkeyCallback`](../type-aliases/HotkeyCallback.md)\n\nThe function to call when the hotkey matches\n\n### options?\n\n[`CreateHotkeyHandlerOptions`](../interfaces/CreateHotkeyHandlerOptions.md) = `{}`\n\nOptions for matching and handling\n\n## Returns\n\nA function that can be used as an event handler\n\n(`event`) => `void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst handler = createHotkeyHandler('Mod+S', (event, { hotkey, parsedHotkey }) => {\n  console.log(`${hotkey} was pressed`)\n  handleSave()\n})\n\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', handler)\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createHotkeyHandler\ntitle: createHotkeyHandler\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createHotkeyHandler(\n   hotkey, \n   callback, \n   options?): (event) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [match.ts:87](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/match.ts#L87)\n\nCreates a keyboard event handler that calls the callback when the hotkey matches.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### hotkey\n\n  \\| [`Hotkey`](../type-aliases/Hotkey.md)\n  \\| [`ParsedHotkey`](../type-aliases/ParsedHotkey.md)\n\nThe hotkey string or ParsedHotkey to match\n\n### callback\n\n[`HotkeyCallback`](../type-aliases/HotkeyCallback.md)\n\nThe function to call when the hotkey matches\n\n### options?\n\n[`CreateHotkeyHandlerOptions`](../interfaces/CreateHotkeyHandlerOptions.md) = `{}`\n\nOptions for matching and handling\n\n## Returns\n\nA function that can be used as an event handler\n\n(`event`) => `void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst handler = createHotkeyHandler('Mod+S', (event, { hotkey, parsedHotkey }) => {\n  console.log(`${hotkey} was pressed`)\n  handleSave()\n})\n\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', handler)\n```\n"}
